## 5. Aim and Objectives

### 5.1 Aim

To design and develop an interactive 3D application, running on **WebGPU** with an optional **WebXR** immersive mode, in which users manipulate objects and light sources to create recognizable shadow patterns and perspective-dependent illusions within a single virtual studio.

### 5.2 Objectives

1. To implement an object manipulation system supporting translation, rotation, scaling, grouping and alignment of 3D primitives and custom glTF meshes.
2. To implement dynamic lighting with multiple, independently controllable and coloured light sources, and to display real-time shadows on a projection surface using custom **WebGPU shadow-mapping passes**.
3. To develop a Shadow Puzzle Mode that compares a generated shadow with a target silhouette, computes a similarity score on the GPU, and offers multiple difficulty levels.
4. To demonstrate anamorphic perspective illusions through camera controls that reveal how an arrangement appears from different viewpoints.
5. To provide a Multi-Light Shadow Studio in which shadows of different colours can be combined into a visual composition.
6. To provide a ShadowArt Creator that allows users to save or capture their compositions.
7. To deliver an immersive **WebXR** mode on supported browsers and headsets, with controller-based selection and manipulation of objects and lights, while keeping the desktop browser experience as the baseline.
8. To apply and document the relevant computer graphics concepts in the implementation, and to deliver a polished, usable application within the project timeline.

