## 12. Risks and Mitigations

| Risk | Impact | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| WebGPU unavailable in a target browser | Application does not start | Capability check at load; clear message; verify on Chrome/Edge and Android Chrome during Phase 2 |
| WebXR/WebGPU composition support varies by headset browser | Immersive mode unavailable or unstable | Commit to one verified browser/headset pair; keep desktop baseline fully functional; test the XR path early in Phase 5 |
| XR frame budget (72/90 Hz) exceeded | Judder and discomfort | Reduce shadow-map resolution and light count in XR; simplify materials; profile with GPU timestamps where available |
| Shadow acne or peter-panning | Silhouettes look incorrect | Tune normal-offset and slope-scaled bias; use PCF and adequate depth precision |
| Scope expansion across six modes plus XR | Core incomplete at deadline | Build the core studio and shadow system first; treat hand tracking, passthrough AR and effects as optional |
| Team learning curve for WGSL and WebXR | Slow early progress | Phase 1 technical spike; pair programming; keep the first pipeline minimal and iterate |
| GPU readback stalls in puzzle scoring | Frame drops during evaluation | Evaluate only on demand; reduce on GPU to one value; use async buffer mapping |

